# Lightning Web Components (LWC) & Salesforce Security Basics

---

# 1. LWC Introduction for Beginners

## What is LWC?

Lightning Web Components (LWC) is a modern JavaScript-based framework used to build fast and reusable UI components in Salesforce.

LWC uses:
- HTML
- JavaScript
- CSS
- Meta XML configuration

It is built on modern web standards and helps developers create responsive Salesforce applications.

---

## Features of LWC
- Fast performance
- Reusable components
- Modern UI development
- Easy integration with Salesforce
- Lightweight architecture

---

## Component Structure in LWC

Each LWC component contains:

### 1. HTML File
Used to design the UI.

Example:
```html
<template>
    <h1>Hello Salesforce</h1>
</template>
```

---

### 2. JavaScript File
Handles logic and functionality.

Example:
```javascript
import { LightningElement } from 'lwc';

export default class HelloWorld extends LightningElement {

}
```

---

### 3. Meta XML File
Controls component configuration and visibility.

Example:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>60.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
</LightningComponentBundle>
```

---

