# 3. Salesforce Security Basics

Salesforce security helps protect organizational data and controls user access.

---

# Profiles and Permissions

## Profiles

Profiles define:
- Object access
- Field permissions
- App visibility
- User capabilities

Example:
- Student profile
- Faculty profile
- Admin profile

---

## Permissions

Permissions control what users can:
- View
- Create
- Edit
- Delete

Examples:
- Faculty can update attendance
- Students can only view their records

---

# Enterprise Security Basics

Enterprise systems require strong security to:
- Protect sensitive data
- Prevent unauthorized access
- Maintain privacy
- Ensure compliance

---

# Salesforce Security Features

| Security Feature | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Profiles | Define user access |
| Permission Sets | Additional permissions |
| Role Hierarchy | Controls record visibility |
| Sharing Rules | Share records securely |
| Field-Level Security | Protect specific fields |

---

# Real-Life Security Example

## Student Management System

### Student Access
Students can:
- View their attendance
- Register for courses
- View notifications

Students cannot:
- Modify faculty records
- Access admin settings

---

### Faculty Access
Faculty can:
- Update attendance
- Manage courses
- View student reports

Faculty cannot:
- Change system-wide settings

---

### Admin Access
Admins can:
- Manage users
- Configure security
- Access all records

---

# Conclusion

Lightning Web Components (LWC) helps developers create modern, fast, and reusable Salesforce applications using HTML, JavaScript, and XML. Salesforce security features like profiles and permissions ensure enterprise applications remain secure, organized, and reliable.
